===Noun===
{{en-noun|illiterac|ies|-}}

# {{uncountable}} The [[inability]] to [[read]].
#: '''''Illiteracy''' is widespread in certain areas of the country.''
# {{uncountable}} The portion of a population unable to read, generally given as a precentage.
#: ''Elbonia has an '''illiteracy''' of 2.5%."
# {{countable}} A denigrated usage (e.g., [[ain't]], [[irregardless]], or the use of the [[double negative]]).
#: ''The use of "an illiteracy" to mean "a mistake" could be considered an '''illiteracy'''.

